        {
          "id": 943977609,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Should we leave `-n` around, just in case somebody has a script that uses it, but deprecate it (e.g., with a warning printed to stderr, noting that `-F pcap` should be used, if `-n` is used)?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
