        {
          "id": 944331644,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Perhaps we should leave it around for at least a release and deprecate it (which was my plan before we decided that the next release was 4.0, since 4.0 is a good time to break things.)\n\nIt's easy to print a warning noting that it's deprecated and has no effect since the default is now pcapng. It doesn't help people with existing scripts that _don't_ use `-n` and are now surprised by getting pcapng instead of pcap, but there's no way for that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
